 Compose window chrome, title/loading state, and a frame around an Android body view.
 
 Gradle module `:xmux-window-frame`; artifact `dev.improve.xmux:xmux-window-frame`.
+
+`WindowChrome.header` optionally replaces the header with app-owned Compose content. It receives
+the live `TerminalWindowState` and the chrome configuration; read Compose state inside this lambda
+to change an existing window's appearance without recreating its terminal view. Keep the custom
+header at `chrome.headerHeightDp` so the spatial panel's sizing and hit testing stay aligned.
+Call `WindowHeader(state, chrome)` to render the default traffic-light header.
